---
name: snowflake-mcp-server-setup
description: >-
  Use when a new owner needs to create a Snowflake-managed MCP server, a
  read-only role, and a PAT so the analyst bot can query their warehouse, or
  when that connection fails.
---
# Set up a Snowflake-managed MCP server (read-only)

Walk the owner through this one step at a time. They run every statement themselves in a Snowsight worksheet as ACCOUNTADMIN; the bot never runs DDL or GRANTs. No semantic model is needed: the SQL execution tool alone is enough (a semantic model is only for the Cortex Analyst tool).

## 1. Home for the server
```sql
USE ROLE ACCOUNTADMIN;
CREATE DATABASE IF NOT EXISTS AI_TOOLS;
CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS AI_TOOLS.MCP;
```

## 2. MCP server with the SQL tool
```sql
CREATE MCP SERVER AI_TOOLS.MCP.ANALYST_MCP
  FROM SPECIFICATION $$
    tools:
      - name: "sql_exec"
        type: "SYSTEM_EXECUTE_SQL"
        description: "Run read-only SQL against the warehouse"
        title: "SQL Execution"
  $$;
```

## 3. Read-only role
```sql
CREATE ROLE IF NOT EXISTS ANALYST_RO;
GRANT USAGE ON WAREHOUSE <wh> TO ROLE ANALYST_RO;
GRANT USAGE ON DATABASE AI_TOOLS TO ROLE ANALYST_RO;
GRANT USAGE ON SCHEMA AI_TOOLS.MCP TO ROLE ANALYST_RO;
GRANT USAGE ON MCP SERVER AI_TOOLS.MCP.ANALYST_MCP TO ROLE ANALYST_RO;
-- for each database they own:
GRANT USAGE ON DATABASE <db> TO ROLE ANALYST_RO;
GRANT USAGE ON ALL SCHEMAS IN DATABASE <db> TO ROLE ANALYST_RO;
GRANT SELECT ON ALL TABLES IN DATABASE <db> TO ROLE ANALYST_RO;
GRANT SELECT ON ALL VIEWS IN DATABASE <db> TO ROLE ANALYST_RO;
GRANT SELECT ON FUTURE TABLES IN DATABASE <db> TO ROLE ANALYST_RO;
-- shared databases take ONE grant instead (individual grants error):
GRANT IMPORTED PRIVILEGES ON DATABASE SNOWFLAKE TO ROLE ANALYST_RO;
GRANT IMPORTED PRIVILEGES ON DATABASE SNOWFLAKE_SAMPLE_DATA TO ROLE ANALYST_RO;
GRANT ROLE ANALYST_RO TO USER <user>;
```

## 4. User defaults and PAT
```sql
ALTER USER <user> SET DEFAULT_WAREHOUSE = <wh>;
CREATE AUTHENTICATION POLICY AI_TOOLS.MCP.PAT_NO_NETPOLICY
  PAT_POLICY = (NETWORK_POLICY_EVALUATION = ENFORCED_NOT_REQUIRED);
ALTER USER <user> SET AUTHENTICATION POLICY AI_TOOLS.MCP.PAT_NO_NETPOLICY;
ALTER USER <user> ADD PROGRAMMATIC ACCESS TOKEN analyst_bot
  ROLE_RESTRICTION = 'ANALYST_RO' DAYS_TO_EXPIRY = 90;
```
The token is shown once; they copy it straight into the secure setup field, never chat. If their org requires network policies, use a network policy allowing the bot's egress instead of the authentication policy.

## 5. URL
Run `SELECT CURRENT_ORGANIZATION_NAME(), CURRENT_ACCOUNT_NAME();` and build:
`https://<org>-<account>.snowflakecomputing.com/api/v2/databases/AI_TOOLS/schemas/MCP/mcp-servers/ANALYST_MCP` (hyphens, not underscores, in the host).

## 6. Connect and verify
Collect the URL and PAT through secure setup fields. Test `tools/list`, then run `SELECT CURRENT_USER(), CURRENT_ROLE(), CURRENT_WAREHOUSE();` and show the result.

## Common errors
- `Granting individual privileges on imported database is not allowed`: shared DB; use `GRANT IMPORTED PRIVILEGES` only.
- `unexpected ''name''`: user names aren't single-quoted. Use `USER name`, or `USER "name"` if it was created lowercase/quoted.
- `User 'X' does not exist`: case mismatch; check `SHOW USERS LIKE '%name%'` and double-quote the exact `name`.
- `Network policy is required` (390432): apply the authentication policy in step 4.
- `warehouse is required but not specified`: set `DEFAULT_WAREHOUSE` on the user.
- `Access denied for trial accounts` (399504): the managed MCP SQL tool doesn't work on trial accounts; the owner must convert to paid in Snowsight billing.

Snowflake changes details over time; confirm against https://docs.snowflake.com/en/user-guide/snowflake-cortex/cortex-agents-mcp.
